{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:59:20.631792Z","id":"467f9c1a2c96cd6da6f7fde24f65d0039c61f89d85be2d6e5e8278bebb82350a","body":{"detail":"Only `flutter build macos --debug` was built, with DebugProfile.entitlements (no sandbox, no keychain group). The Release target uses this file with the project's ad hoc identity; macOS requires a provisioning profile for keychain-access-groups, so a Release build may be killed on launch by amfid until it is signed with a team identity. flutter_secure_storage needs the group to store the API key in the sandboxed app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"efa97308a88e35f883cbfe3d5224dea64d0c21a7a94b3b46f973d3c4fe7780c5"},"suggested_fix":"Build and launch the Release app once (V1); if it is refused, sign with a team identity or drop the group for local builds.","summary":"keychain-access-groups is a restricted entitlement: a Release build signed ad hoc (CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY \"-\") may be refused at launch","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:04:07.305024Z","id":"a3db09a4c6e4f331c98204b99bd160a150a5a2dcceddef6b4aa33ae99f2cb2db","body":{"detail":"flutter_secure_storage 11.2.0 (pubspec.lock) defaults MacOsOptions.usesDataProtectionKeychain to true (lib/options/macos_options.dart in the package; flutter_secure_storage_darwin 0.4.3 FlutterSecureStorage.swift:285 then sets kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain). Writes to that keychain need a keychain-access-groups entitlement and a signing team; this file has none and the Debug Runner is signed ad hoc (CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY \"-\" in macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj), so the API key read and write on the macOS Debug build are expected to fail with errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018). Not run: nothing reads or writes the key yet. The Release side of the same entitlement is record 467f9c1a on macos/Runner/Release.entitlements.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"53b6faa8ed2e1b87f1c79671af7fe065933c3b314dc117e5b180590251e91e7e"},"suggested_fix":"Where the SecureKey is built for macOS, pass `MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false)` for builds without the sandbox (the login keychain needs no entitlement), or give Debug a team and the access group; cover it with a write-then-read check on the macOS build.","summary":"flutter_secure_storage on macOS defaults to the data protection keychain, which needs a keychain-access-groups entitlement the Debug build does not have","tags":["review","macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:07:37.346880Z","id":"0345c880fd1f93233280241f94f1507de9f75f4bcc20564533eda1abe1d76ba1","body":{"detail":"xcodebuild: `\"Runner\" has entitlements that require signing with a development certificate. Enable development signing in the Signing & Capabilities editor.` (BUILD FAILED). The same Release build with keychain-access-groups removed from the entitlements succeeds. A Release macOS build needs a team identity, or the group dropped for local builds.","kind":"comment","references":"467f9c1a2c96cd6da6f7fde24f65d0039c61f89d85be2d6e5e8278bebb82350a","summary":"Confirmed at build time: `flutter build macos --release` fails before launch","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:10:56.103042Z","id":"8c37e781745868692b5756ebb69fc591d8b4fc24103233e27f57cfbc998bf2ad","body":{"detail":"`flutter build macos --release` in apps/clax_app: `✓ Built build/macos/Build/Products/Release/clax_app.app (73.6MB)`, exit 0. The Release binary started in the background stayed alive 5 s and exited 143 on SIGTERM to its PID. `codesign -d --entitlements -` on Contents/Resources/clax shows app-sandbox and inherit; on the app, app-sandbox, device.audio-input, network.client and network.server; `codesign --verify --deep --strict` passes. tool/sandbox_probe.dart built as the Release entry point (`flutter build macos --release -t tool/sandbox_probe.dart`) printed: sandbox container dev.empathic.clax, `--version: exit 0, clax 0.4.0`, serve on a free loopback port with CLAX_HOME in the container, `healthz: 200`, `serve exit: 0`, PASS (exit 0). The API key's storage without an access group is on thread a3db09a4.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d9b5c984","summary":"Release.entitlements no longer carries keychain-access-groups; `flutter build macos --release` succeeds and the sandboxed app runs clax","supersedes":"467f9c1a2c96cd6da6f7fde24f65d0039c61f89d85be2d6e5e8278bebb82350a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:10:56.103235Z","id":"49a69b2fc62b928af00869c82f28ebe1737bf9216f539b6a361bd83c5e46ad8e","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Release.entitlements dropped keychain-access-groups (commit d9b5c984), because it is a restricted entitlement that the ad hoc signed Release build cannot carry. The SecureKey implementation (lib/platform/secure_key.dart, FlutterSecureStorage key \"anthropic_api_key\") must construct FlutterSecureStorage with `mOptions: MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false)` so macOS uses the login keychain, which needs no access group, in Debug and Release alike. Spec §3.2 in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md states this.","kind":"comment","references":"a3db09a4c6e4f331c98204b99bd160a150a5a2dcceddef6b4aa33ae99f2cb2db","summary":"Neither macOS entitlements file has a keychain group now: the key store must pass MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false)","tags":["requirement","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:36.587278Z","id":"16d036b29bc1d7c70033d331261896ff553dc779aa486aa80c040a64cd7f56c1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8b8dff15","summary":"The key store builds FlutterSecureStorage with MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false) (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart, FlutterSecureKey.macOsOptions; test/ui/settings_test.dart 'the key store uses the login keychain on macOS' passes). tool/secure_key_probe.dart, which writes, reads back and deletes a probe value with those options under its own storage key, printed 'write ok / read matches / delete ok / PASS' (exit 0) built with flutter build macos --debug (no app-sandbox entitlement) and again with --release (codesign shows app-sandbox).","supersedes":"a3db09a4c6e4f331c98204b99bd160a150a5a2dcceddef6b4aa33ae99f2cb2db","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631392Z","id":"593bc01d88fa804f2f00a83f6c0935e0384799f93672b42ee8e9c2a76f19e563","body":{"detail":"macOS has no ringer switch the app can read, and Focus state is not readable without extra entitlements, so play Tink/Pop at volume 0.6 of the output; a muted output plays nothing. Android (CuesChannel.kt silenced()) skips the tone for silent, vibrate, zero notification volume and Do Not Disturb. The channel lives in MainFlutterWindow.swift rather than its own CuesChannel.swift so that Runner.xcodeproj needs no new file reference.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"0a6b8e9df1d888618e46487852ddfed486f439496592c95b46eaf7674d1e05b5"},"summary":"macOS cues play whatever Focus or mute state the Mac is in, at output volume","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:50:09.005625Z","id":"bc48d382986138a09acf1ed808e40813cad4db7e11b2792811c6cb1c2c56d70d","body":{"detail":"AppDelegate.swift typechecks against FlutterMacOS (xcrun swiftc -typecheck) but the app was not built after the Info.plist UTExportedTypeDeclarations/CFBundleDocumentTypes change. Unverified: Finder opening a .clax in Clax at cold start (the channel is installed in applicationWillFinishLaunching from mainFlutterWindow; a nil controller there would drop the cold-start file into pendingBundles with no channel until the next open), and sandbox read access to the opened path from Dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"9a35917583e696813c7e4806a420a9c8f15732de0637f9775fd33d45822d925e"},"summary":"The macOS document type and application(_:open:) delivery are unbuilt and unexercised","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:31:38.428819Z","id":"b253c18882b350fa28f8a1c732b9db9722dfe1e321020a44e7283c13882dc64b","body":{"detail":"The Bazel-built Clax.app (//apps/clax_app:macos_app at 0c1b42af) launched and made its window, but this session had no permission to send Apple Events to System Events (osascript error -1743) and screencapture -l failed ('could not create image from window'), so Clax > About Clax was never chosen and the panel never captured. target/flutter-app/shots/about-mac-{light,dark}.png were drawn by a scratch program that calls NSApp.orderFrontStandardAboutPanel with the built app's Info.plist name, version, copyright and icon and About.credits over its haiku.json: they show 'Clax', 'Version 1.0.0 (1)', a haiku in grey serif italic and 'Copyright (C) 2026 Empathic, Inc.'. macos_app_test checks the compiled MainMenu.nib names showAbout: and 'About Clax'. Unverified: the menu item reaching AppDelegate.showAbout: through the nib's target, and a new haiku on a second opening while the panel is already up. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §7.4's Option-click on the About haiku for another is not built here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"46d199714ae17efaf22eaf80edb34cce644b538307f5d7537a894ce61fbce84c"},"suggested_fix":"On a Mac with Accessibility allowed for the terminal, open the Bazel-built app with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR, choose Clax > About Clax twice, and capture the panel with screencapture -l<window ID>.","summary":"About Clax was not opened from the menu of the running app; the About render comes from a harness","tags":["needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/NativeDialogs.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:33:08.474051Z","id":"2b8009b0e2ae8a647077a72961a72bfbebb8e92a328afa020b192d76766335bd","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_dialogs_test checks isHeldReturn on synthesized events and that the default button is disabled until the injected schedule fires, and a scratch AppKit harness running AlertRun as a sheet confirmed the view tree (Allow disabled before arming and enabled after, 'Always allow' after the suppression button is clicked, dismissAlert answering the cancel index). Not verified: that the local keyDown monitor swallows a held Return on a real key sheet, that a fresh Return after arming presses the default (the harness process could not become active, so the sheet never took keys), and how the sheet looks (screencapture -l has no screen-recording permission from an agent shell; cacheDisplay and dataWithPDF of the sheet render blank). The capability prompt from the kit example's net call has not been seen in the built Clax.app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":290},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"a4ba05afc89b21685c6fc65ea92e634c62cb9c2e90b68eaeb22cdf85041350d6"},"suggested_fix":"Drive the built app (scratch CLAX_HOME) to a capability prompt and capture the window before and after arming, as the macOS chrome test does for its states; press and hold Return across the arming.","summary":"The armed alert's keys and its pixels are unverified in a running app","tags":["verification","macos","native-overlays","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/NativeDialogs.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:33:08.475488Z","id":"1d5f6e83889cc39b85110c21dea16ce2bc8c5f4a8f30ede18924d8fd5166b76f","body":{"detail":"NSMenuItem.subtitle is macOS 14.4+; on macOS 12–14.3 the detail (such as the model name of a choice in Settings, lib/ui/settings_screen.dart:744) is dropped from the native menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"217163049e979ac06320c791bd7ee194a8a173346366db037aad9a5a593cae09"},"suggested_fix":"Before 14.4, append the detail to an attributedTitle in secondaryLabelColor.","summary":"A menu item's detail shows only on macOS 14.4 and later","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/EditBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.832702Z","id":"f7f77ff562d5807e069ba6faef726e58db3e57f0548453e768bef4c03020f4fb","body":{"detail":"Checked: the compiled nib item by item (tool/macos-app-check.sh, macos_app_test), the Dart side over mock channels (test/ui/app_menu_test.dart, test/ui/shortcuts_test.dart), and that the built Clax.app launches and shows its window with MenuBridge and EditBridge installed. Not checked: that AppKit sends ⌘C, ⌘V, ⌘Z to EditBridge while a Flutter TextField has the focus rather than Flutter's own shortcuts taking them first (either way the field gets them); that flutterHasFocus sees a WKWebView first responder as a page (the walk up superviews); that Edit's items validate through NSApp.target(forAction:) for a page; that the claxMenuAction: key equivalents (⌘K, ⌘[, ⇧⌘H) fire while a page has the focus. screencapture and System Events were not permitted in the session that built it, so no menu-*.png exists. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.8 asks for an integration test of ⌘C and ⌘V in a page field and in a Flutter field; none exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"69ad5b01e8a6ed8a8280e1090513f7d220ce5961495b6b523c6353f7d8b04964"},"suggested_fix":"Add the integration test (integration_test/, dev.empathic.clax/test-input can be extended to send key events) and capture each menu into target/flutter-app/shots/menu-*.png.","summary":"The native menu bar and both bridges are unverified in a running app: no menu was opened, no key equivalent pressed, no ⌘C/⌘V tried in a page or a Flutter field","tags":["needs-verification","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.832747Z","id":"cc237a21cecaff1161b00ce64927e5cefda2b544a24e4ff2f2e23b7873c8641b","body":{"detail":"The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.8) says Clax Help opens the docs but names no URL, and nothing in the repository names a documentation site; the GitHub path follows the release URL in the README (github.com/empathic/clax).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"d3f805871ee1bf0349e80fed35bf72656dd639647cf65a2a0ca3b52d1be6cf3e"},"summary":"Help › Clax Help opens https://github.com/empathic/clax/tree/main/docs, a guess at where Clax's documentation lives","tags":["status:needs-decision","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:37:08.808108Z","id":"1db794ad5b4213c94170c069fe1dbe53533a1774df4407206fb39612315614c3","body":{"detail":"ClaxEngine.shared calls enableMultiView through responds(to:) and perform before the engine's first view controller, and runs the engine before making one (a view added to an engine that is not running is refused: 'FlutterEngineAddView returned kInvalidArguments'). Without enableMultiView a second FlutterViewController on the engine throws NSInternalInconsistencyException 'The engine already has a view controller for the implicit view'. The selector is in FlutterMacOS.framework's binary but in no public header, and Flutter's own windowing turns multi-view on the same way. Under multi-view the main window is view 1 and Dart's implicit view 0 is an empty phantom, so lib/app.dart runClaxApp uses runWidget with ClaxViews (lib/ui/mac/windows.dart). If the selector is missing the app logs it and runs one window; the fallback for Settings and the Inbox is then window sheets on the main window.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"32562d432565f842edba5059853ce947b9967d2b80f5d98019be753003d0078c"},"summary":"Further windows are FlutterViewControllers on the one engine in multi-view mode, turned on by the private -[FlutterEngine enableMultiView]; Flutter's RegularWindowController (flag-gated, @internal in 3.47.7) was not used","tags":["macos","private-api","revisit:windowing is public in a pinned Flutter, enableMultiView is renamed or removed, or the owner wants the Mac App Store","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:37:08.808167Z","id":"a71399f742f5d30e7b2e851d5a7084b2132b5358e55fae60e23888f83c159bad","body":{"detail":"Outside the App Store a private Objective-C selector on a bundled framework is no obstacle to notarization. For the App Store, App Review's guideline 2.5.1 allows public APIs only; the alternative is one window with Settings and the Inbox as window sheets on it (no enableMultiView, ClaxViews keeps a single view). Decision needed before Task 49 builds the Settings and Inbox windows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"32562d432565f842edba5059853ce947b9967d2b80f5d98019be753003d0078c"},"summary":"Mac distribution: the app calls the private -[FlutterEngine enableMultiView], which Mac App Store review may refuse; is the Mac app distributed outside the App Store (Developer ID, notarized), or must it pass App Store review?","tags":["macos","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:37:08.808197Z","id":"a60253b9303ded758fa8b5b2221fea4acb74b7520e44bccdd3fd899e3ff41879","body":{"detail":"The legacy single-view accessors read the implicit view 0, which no window shows. share_plus force-unwraps registrar.view (SharePlusMacosPlugin.swift:35-40 in share_plus 13.3.1), so a page's share on the Mac goes through MacShare (lib/platform/device/mac_share.dart, the 'share' method of dev.empathic.clax/native) instead, and share_plus must stay unused on macOS (PluginBundleFiles uses file_picker there, toFile true). file_selector_macos (FileSelectorPlugin.swift:71) and file_picker pass a nil window and run their panels modal for the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"364eef031872a4fb799d7b901372d524a4e401fb7914f07bc1b4d9156c3e1a85"},"suggested_fix":"Show the save and open panels from Runner code as sheets on the window of the calling view, as NativeDialogs does for alerts.","summary":"Under multi-view registrar.view and engine.viewController are nil: file panels from file_picker and file_selector_macos open app-modal rather than as sheets, and share_plus's macOS plugin would crash","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:37:08.808232Z","id":"1433f902e3ea7fe8f58a69a2075a72b808b288a06ecbe9defbfc0456dc55774b","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_window_bridge_test covers WindowBridge, SidebarView and SidebarContainer in an offscreen window, and the Dart tests cover the channels. A run of the built app with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR made one 1200x800 window, centred and saved as 'NSWindow Frame ClaxMain', but the screen was locked and the app never active, so nothing was seen: not the transparent unified title bar, not the content padded below it, not the sidebar material (no Dart code sets a sidebar width before Task 46), not Escape pressed in a page with the panel open, not ⌘C in a field after switching windows, not a page's share. The daemon did not start in that run: its start waited on a login-keychain prompt for the saved API key, which an ad hoc signed build raises.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"a19a070837640b23be7e0cc59b19a6ffe18efd5198537fdd87334ce6a5c92d31"},"summary":"The main window's chrome, the sidebar material, the Escape monitor, window focus forwarding and the native share picker are unverified in a running app","tags":["macos","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:37:08.808265Z","id":"87732376e0a4fc1edce70eb9e20d60272949eff7f26d286a82ef11ffc5ba8cdd","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":209},"content_hash":"1e1922936f9d4b5802d67c0b3cc440b4a9c8202ca33006791b6b990974c22cb6"},"suggested_fix":"Have scripts/sync-tokens.py write the colour into a generated Swift file, or have Dart send it with setSidebarWidth.","summary":"SidebarView's solid colour under Reduce Transparency copies design/tokens.json's bg by hand, and //design:tokens_sync does not check it","tags":["macos","tokens","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:32:45.868400Z","id":"f1ea4b0d84de33e55bdfb78cb619079b80b29ec35ca75a911ea494ef082d7c5d","body":{"detail":"test/ui/mac/traffic_lights_test.dart assumes a 52-point row with the zoom button's right edge at 74 points (WindowTitlebar(top: 52, leading: 74)) and checks the Flutter side only; WindowBridgeTests checks that Titlebar(of:) reports the zoom button's edge. The Bazel macos_app built at c856de01e launched with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory, but screencapture -l and -R both failed ('could not create image from window/rect': no screen recording permission here), so the row was not seen. Unchecked: that the empty toolbar gives the row and centres the buttons on this macOS; that Back and the actions in the row take clicks rather than the title bar; that the row still drags the window where Flutter draws nothing (FlutterView may take those mouse-downs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"e2526619facf8375fd4974eeda8dfd528120804c6211607ceb7951ca944b799d"},"suggested_fix":"Run the app, look at the top-left corner of the inbox, settings and a thread, click Back in the row, and drag the window by an empty part of the row; if the row does not drag, have WindowBridge call performDrag for mouse-downs Flutter reports as unhandled in the row.","summary":"The toolbar row (empty NSToolbar, hidden title) is unverified in a running app: its height, the window buttons' place and whether clicks in the row reach Flutter","tags":["macos","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:24.066010Z","id":"4a5f7823e036cc04058bca66a35f829232a559bc8041f15a504e865bb314513e","body":{"detail":"Checked by //apps/clax_app:macos_toolbar_test (items, order, groups, in-place updates, clicks by calling the item actions) and by an offscreen render: the real MacToolbar over the Mac rig's open-app PNG, drawn with cacheDisplay (target/flutter-app/shots/mac-app-toolbar-{light,dark}.png). In light the capsules, symbols, title and subtitle and the badge draw as expected; in dark the glass capsules came out white with the symbols invisible, which may be the offscreen render not resolving Liquid Glass rather than the app. No screen recording or accessibility permission was available here, so no real click reached an item; NSToolbarItemGroup's action reading selectedIndex is unexercised with a real segment click; the share picker finds the item's button by its accessibility label (WindowToolbar.anchor), with a fallback under the toolbar's trailing end.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"bb7e2496c3c5f314d9cf00b8e929b4c52d0c9f74c23d4ea82f27de2aa5899039"},"suggested_fix":"Run the built app in light and dark, open an app, click Back, Comment, Threads and Share (the picker should hang from the Share button), and capture the toolbar.","summary":"The native toolbar is unverified in a running, focused app: clicks on its items, the share picker's anchor, and its dark appearance","tags":["macos","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:24.066112Z","id":"de5ebdc87ca80f45407d2ae1ee2b9215dc0f3c21025594af767c0cc048cccba1","body":{"detail":"FlutterView is opaque (mouseDownCanMoveWindow is false), so AppKit never moves the window by the row where Flutter draws; a probe confirmed a press in an empty-toolbar row hit-tests to the content view. WindowRowDrag (lib/ui/mac/window_drag.dart) calls MacWindow.dragWindow when its recognizer wins, and WindowBridge.dragWindow calls performDrag(with:) on the press its local monitor kept, if the button is still down, or the title bar's double click action on a second click. test/ui/mac/window_drag_test.dart and WindowDragTests check each side alone; whether performDrag started a channel round trip after mouse-down follows the mouse smoothly, and whether the double click arrives before the button comes up, is untested.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"603b4de287ebada8f4a683b764ec76e371d2e1e1a3d19ff6abb13a5015eea1fd"},"suggested_fix":"In the built app, drag the window by the empty part of the inbox's and the launcher's row, and double-click it.","summary":"Dragging the window by the Flutter-drawn toolbar row is unverified with a real mouse: performDrag runs from a kept mouse-down after Dart's gesture arena answers over the channel","tags":["macos","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:35.441826Z","id":"278f14132b26d85cd942524619d937023075c7695b77791bbf805091afc1c339","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aec7debcd","summary":"Fixed: the row is measured and clicks and drags in it are handled. An offscreen window with the icon-only unified toolbar (Toolbar.swift's MacToolbar.attach) measures 52 points high with the zoom button's right edge at 79, which test/ui/mac/traffic_lights_test.dart now uses; a press in the empty row hit-tests to the content view, so Flutter gets clicks there, but FlutterView is opaque and never moves the window, which WindowRowDrag plus WindowBridge's dragWindow now do. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_mac_window_drag_test //apps/clax_app:ui_mac_traffic_lights_test //apps/clax_app:macos_window_bridge_test PASSED. A real mouse is still untried: record fc4ae3de.","supersedes":"f1ea4b0d84de33e55bdfb78cb619079b80b29ec35ca75a911ea494ef082d7c5d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Camera.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:40:45.917598Z","id":"ecf53a16e067c439cb50b9eb8e52cff0e4858066abc391e496120c446b658183","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_camera_test checks CameraBridge's answers with the system and the sheet stood in for, the JPEG downscale (CameraBridge.jpeg, 3200x2400 to 1600x1200) and the sheet's buttons and keys without starting a session; test/platform/device/mac_camera_test.dart checks MacCamera over a mock channel. Unchecked: the sheet's look in light and dark, the live preview (AVCaptureVideoPreviewLayer as the view's layer, aspect fill at 4:3), Take Photo turning on at AVCaptureSessionDidStartRunning, AVCapturePhotoOutput's JPEG and its orientation (no mirroring is applied, so a front camera's photo is unmirrored while some Mac apps mirror the preview), the camera prompt with NSCameraUsageDescription, the sheet landing on the window whose page asked (it uses NSApp.keyWindow), only the default video device being offered (no camera picker for an external camera), and an ad hoc signed build keeping the camera grant across rebuilds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":334},"content_hash":"e44543c551f231689c2964d95d143cdcb60e38252ff4917125496562a0214738"},"summary":"The Mac's capture sheet is unverified in a running app: no camera was opened, no permission prompt answered, no photo taken","tags":["unverified","device","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:54:45.736069Z","id":"fdd51ac2e583d878334241a01a44570a12d75dbffb0063bb0d85d60bf19103ba","body":{"detail":"The spacer's width is the sidebar's edge less its own leading x in the window (SidebarEdgeView.width), recomputed on its frame changes, window resizes and full-screen changes. ToolbarTests checks the identifiers and the width from a placed view, not a laid-out NSToolbar; the gap after it is whatever AppKit puts between items. NSTrackingSeparatorToolbarItem was not used: it needs an NSSplitView, and the split is drawn by Flutter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":416},"end":{"line":475},"content_hash":"2a72e5fd96ee078b7e7a98deba458d34a7c99945cadfca58f178f8170178b1c6"},"suggested_fix":"In the running app (Task 52's chrome test), capture the toolbar with the sidebar at 180, 220 and 320 wide and in full screen, and check that Back starts past the divider.","summary":"SidebarEdgeView is checked only by unit tests: where AppKit lays it out in a shown window, the item spacing after it, and full screen (no window buttons) are unverified","tags":["macos","split","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:14:04.757394Z","id":"e0304c0e2df58d02e0f3449de66684de4055a697b6933d2b66085ca53c2abd2f","body":{"detail":"ToolbarTests sets the field's text and calls searchChanged; it does not lay out a shown NSToolbar. ⌘F is Edit › Find…'s key equivalent (MainMenu.xib, performFindPanelAction:): with the Flutter view first responder the key reaches SplitShell's shortcut, but with the home page's WKWebView first responder the menu item may go to the page's find instead, so ⌘F may not reach the toolbar's field after a click in the grid.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":290},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"e8e5a2f2d6747e776c8d931be6f6a7869e4a02c201b2f42148c64b9f5f840f43"},"summary":"The toolbar's search field is checked only by unit tests: its width and place after Threads in a shown window, typing into it, Escape and its clear button, and ⌘F while the home page's WKWebView has the keyboard are unverified","tags":["macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:02.598307Z","id":"5247df7d9381f96a52e7f6dfaa60aa11655f7a489de9dae5f30b653b02a50555","body":{"detail":"Checked by unit tests only: //apps/clax_app:macos_window_bridge_test (open, setContentHeight), //apps/clax_app:macos_toolbar_test (selectable items, the preference style), //apps/clax_app:ui_settings_tabs_test, //apps/clax_app:ui_inbox_split_test, //apps/clax_app:app_test, and the renders of //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_settings_tabs_shots_test and //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_inbox_split_shots_test, whose toolbars are stand-ins. //apps/clax_app:macos_app builds. The session that built them could not capture the screen ('screencapture -R0,0,400,300' answered 'could not create image from rect') or send key events (osascript: 'Not authorized to send Apple events to System Events'), so no window was opened or captured, light or dark.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"cb2a79eba59e110da1443928eabc68bef6809e094513dda08d02c6163b4a0525"},"suggested_fix":"Open both windows in the macOS chrome test (plan Task 52's TestChannel: captureWindow, setAppearance) and capture each Settings tab and the Inbox window, light and dark; close each and check its view leaves PlatformDispatcher.views.","summary":"The Settings and Inbox windows are unverified in a running app: a further FlutterViewController on the shared engine, the preference toolbar's tabs and their clicks, the height fitted per tab, the Inbox toolbar's segmented control and search, ⌘, and ⇧⌘I, and closing a window letting go of its view","tags":["macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:02.598424Z","id":"0bc795ebfc2c879db2c2bffbdc497af0c52b67b1bcf77abaa85db0fc3579947e","body":{"detail":"setFrameUsingName(\"ClaxSettings\") restores the last frame, height included; setContentSize keeps the frame's origin (its bottom left), so the top moves by the difference until SettingsTabs reports the tab's height and WindowBridge.setContentHeight (which keeps the top) resizes it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"6648fde9a639f1787b1ad77e967d43f2c38a71cb57ac61fa6f2840e6d8f7953a"},"suggested_fix":"Restore only the saved top-left point, or set the content height keeping frame.maxY as setContentHeight does.","summary":"A Settings window opened again restores its saved frame, then takes a 420 point content height anchored at the bottom, so its top edge can jump before Dart fits the tab","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:02.598649Z","id":"20bf466c28cc93b5cfbb4193e90939a01713ea7c53b5855ae83edf194efbdb96","body":{"detail":"MenuBridge's currentView is windows.mainView so that Settings… and Inbox stay enabled and run while a further window is key (the main window's ClaxMenuBar enables them for its view). Commands that only make sense in the main window are neither disabled nor sent elsewhere while Settings or the Inbox is key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"653fca395ce55ccf108ae345f6034ee629ea4f82d7622b957d768bf04da70951"},"suggested_fix":"Send the key window's kind with each command and disable the main window's own commands (Comment, Show Threads, Back, Reload, Home) while a further window is key.","summary":"The menu bar always acts on the main window, also while Settings or the Inbox is in front: View › Comment, Show Threads, Back and Home act on the window behind","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:02.599953Z","id":"cdfee021c4b430e1ed016cb650edc628173932b20f6d420abaf7a232381e54ef","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a71399f742f5d30e7b2e851d5a7084b2132b5358e55fae60e23888f83c159bad","summary":"Settings and the Inbox now open as windows of their own on this multi-view engine (apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift openWindow, commit 1ada66541), so the decision still stands open: under App Store review they would go back to window sheets on the main window, and AppRoot without WindowContents (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart runClaxApp) already shows both as screens of the main window.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:22:19.713852Z","id":"8a6ec2aabc5248da54398091e9f348791369b420424155bcfb77bb62d6adf89c","body":{"detail":"macos_window_bridge_test checks the answer and the push with an injected colour; apps/clax_app/test/ui/hover_test.dart checks the Dart side over a mock channel. Nothing has run the built app and changed the accent. Check: run the Mac app with a scratch CLAX_HOME, focus the sidebar, change the accent and the Multicolor/Graphite setting, and see the selected row and a focused push button follow in both appearances.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"2dadc30559d66bec654ecdb27c6e1fc34ebe1aa16a18bb9e7bb3f9f1d02c0ec9"},"summary":"The system accent is unverified in a running app: accentColor's answer, the systemColorsDidChangeNotification push, and that every open window (main, Settings, Inbox) repaints when System Settings › Appearance › Accent colour changes","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.975664Z","id":"6b7df994e3538b3cf9cdd7736f2827f5d1be3f9b31c4aaec987e1861cb71acdf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fdd51ac2e583d878334241a01a44570a12d75dbffb0063bb0d85d60bf19103ba","summary":"Laid out in the running app the spacer had gone to the toolbar's trailing end with no width: from macOS 14 only navigational items lead and the rest trail. c4e08f64f makes the items over the sidebar and the spacer navigational; bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md) then reports the spacer ending at 220 with the sidebar ending at 220, and target/flutter-app/mac/app-light.png shows Hide Sidebar over the sidebar and Back, Forward and the title over the detail. Still unverified: full screen, and the gap AppKit puts after the spacer on a display (the run's layout was forced with layoutSubtreeIfNeeded).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.975911Z","id":"2917363836658d3363d4f3590e0c223eb04b366a69d09eddabfee282cdd74c7f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e0304c0e2df58d02e0f3449de66684de4055a697b6933d2b66085ca53c2abd2f","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): at Home the toolbar lists Comment, Threads, Refresh, then the search field (325 points wide at x 877 of a 1210-point window), and home-light.png shows it at the trailing end. Typing into it, Escape, its clear button and ⌘F with the home page focused need an active app and stay unverified.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.976129Z","id":"64d5d5e11b6fb7d31ec6252d4ff1b1465b7cda8814a01ffd26d88fc87cd29b3f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5247df7d9381f96a52e7f6dfaa60aa11655f7a489de9dae5f30b653b02a50555","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): Clax › Settings… and Window › Inbox (chosen as a click on the item does) open both windows as further views; each of the seven Settings tabs is selected through its toolbar item's action and drawn (settings-<tab>-light/dark.png, the window's height following the tab); the Inbox's toolbar has the All/Unread/Questions group, Mark all read and its search field (inbox-light.png). Still unverified: ⌘, and ⇧⌘I as key presses, a real click on a tab or segment, and closing a window letting go of its view. In the layer-drawn captures a further window's Flutter content can lag one appearance switch behind (settings-claude-dark.png shows light content): its view draws no new frame while no display shows it.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.976339Z","id":"275644afe47ad47d426c09da668773e1a7762f861a174d413afe734cf089e166","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8a6ec2aabc5248da54398091e9f348791369b420424155bcfb77bb62d6adf89c","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md), launched with -AppleAccentColor 5: accentColor answers purple (light #953d96, dark #a550a7), the sidebar's selected row is purple in app-light/dark.png and make-light.png, and MacWindow.accent is pushed again after NSColor.systemColorsDidChangeNotification. Still unverified: changing the accent in System Settings while the app runs and every open window repainting.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.977852Z","id":"57a13592c29ddcde8f75ccadc925c5802e91f72e47e078aaec48b1366418c062","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4a5f7823e036cc04058bca66a35f829232a559bc8041f15a504e865bb314513e","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): Comment, Threads and the Settings tabs were clicked through their items' actions (as AppKit sends them) and the app answered; app-light.png shows the items. Still unverified: a real mouse click and a segment click, the share picker's anchor (macOS 26 draws items in hosting views, not NSButtons, so WindowToolbar.anchor's button search may find none), and the dark appearance: drawn from layers the glass capsules come out white in dark, as the earlier offscreen render did.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/NativeDialogs.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.978071Z","id":"72b2a8c5ff57c6401c738511b42a11e90ddf9c441d2eef0d662e8995b7c8c4d4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2b8009b0e2ae8a647077a72961a72bfbebb8e92a328afa020b192d76766335bd","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): alert-waiting-light/dark.png show the sheet with Allow disabled and the Always checkbox, alert-armed-light/dark.png with Allow enabled. The held and fresh Return are checked only when the app is active, and were skipped.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/EditBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.978289Z","id":"602c7eea364127cabd5aaba710fdfe7702067b1c1643ed535ee5b199ea0f669d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f7f77ff562d5807e069ba6faef726e58db3e57f0548453e768bef4c03020f4fb","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): the menu bar's items, key equivalents and Clax items' enabled state match apps/clax_app/integration_test/goldens/main_menu.txt; each top-level menu popped up and closed (its PNG blank: a locked display composites nothing); Settings…, Inbox and New App… reached Dart when chosen. ⌘C and ⌘V in a page and a Flutter field, and key equivalents, need an active app and were skipped.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.978508Z","id":"e156c0e9ec12ea7570266f53e96991ec93fe6217540c84bf123fe4f773bebc51","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1433f902e3ea7fe8f58a69a2075a72b808b288a06ecbe9defbfc0456dc55774b","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): the transparent unified title bar with the content under it shows in the captures. Still unverified: the sidebar material, the Escape monitor with a real key, focus forwarding between windows and the page's share.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/TestChannel.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.978797Z","id":"9db76d5bd972f10e4d1c90b4fc3f2d1787254729040e752ebaaad5009ab78ea1","body":{"detail":"compose() draws the window's background colour where NSVisualEffectView materials are, cacheDisplay of the title bar draws the toolbar's glass capsules white in dark, menus (separate windows the window server composites) come out one flat colour, and a Settings or Inbox view draws no new frame while no display shows it, so its IOSurface can still hold the previous appearance (target/flutter-app/mac/settings-claude-dark.png showed light content). make-light.png also showed two crosshair shapes in the content not seen in any widget render; their source is unknown. Captures from the screen (an unlocked, awake display) have none of these.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":385},"end":{"line":482},"content_hash":"2d46c87e67285242e679dbc13418c81c0e321e2e4fac5d43b099eb21b9982874"},"summary":"A window drawn from its layers (a locked or sleeping display) differs from the screen: materials and Liquid Glass are missing or white, menus are blank, and a further window's Flutter content can lag an appearance switch","tags":["macos","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/TestChannel.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.978841Z","id":"3112462c77f52ce663d93fb2bec55e4193a7acafa372a1c78b38e491e21418de","body":{"detail":"deliver() calls the hit view's mouseDown/mouseDragged/mouseUp and the window's key handling, running WindowBridge.mouseDown and escape as the local monitors would. AppKit routes a real drag's release to the view that took its press the same way, but WebKit may treat these events differently (no user activation for picks, as integration_test/rig.dart's comment notes). mac_chrome_test.dart asserts the real pick, the area release, Escape, ⌘C/⌘V and the armed Return only when the events were queued through AppKit (an active app).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":701},"end":{"line":742},"content_hash":"28ef35a81a6db33b6555cdfc6968fbfcca6086970442f92c001b0ce634aabae1"},"summary":"With Clax inactive, events go to their views directly: they skip AppKit's first-mouse rules and the event monitors but the Escape one, so a drag, pick or key checked that way is not a person's","tags":["macos","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.878007Z","id":"f3218c17f4d31eb4c02f8dc5d8452be9d79274b12171047123845a0453c581aa","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_scheme_spike (integration_test/scheme_spike.dart, phase 3), first of two runs on 2026-10-20: the content frame fetched and loaded as an image clax://app/spike.html while the shell reloaded. Two of its requests came before the policy opened the permit and were answered 403; the next request for the URL whose mainDocumentURL was that URL (the frame's: a subresource's mainDocumentURL is the top document's) took navigation 3 and was answered with the shell, and the reload's own request got 403, which is what committed (CLAX_SPIKE_NOTE race: pageNonce empty, bodyText 'refused'). In the second run the reload's own request came first and the shell came back under its own nonce. Spec section 4.4 'What remains' accepts this residual; the spike shows it happens readily once a page makes such requests during a reload (one run in two, eight fetch-and-image rounds), not only in a narrow race. Only the content policy (default-src, connect-src) stops a page from making them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"f230f3e64c8a60fc27f1ab6aa5d81f25e2ab8547c01d1c90015106fd3ac86f52"},"summary":"On the Mac, a page fetching the shell page's URL during the shell's reload took the reload's navigation number in one of two spike runs, so that load had no shell","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.370310Z","id":"eb403f0b7a8781766d5ec1c4fc48b81cd35376bd15707f4bb98dc55e1404a5a0","body":{"detail":"Fix designed in the suggestion on docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:607-624 (permit open until commit, a nonce per matching request); baseline rate: 0 of 25 Mac runs lost the reload on 2026-10-20 (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_scheme_spike --runs_per_test=5, then --runs_per_test=20 --nocache_test_results); in every run the frame's 16 requests were all answered 403 with no number and the navigation's own request came last (CLAX_SPIKE_NOTE race), i.e. the burst ended before the policy opened the permit and the window was never exercised. The run of record f3218c17 that lost it was 1 of 2","kind":"comment","references":"f3218c17f4d31eb4c02f8dc5d8452be9d79274b12171047123845a0453c581aa","summary":"Fix designed on the spec's 'What remains' paragraph; the current spike measured 0 of 25 runs lost, because its race never reaches the window","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371169Z","id":"46cd022052a554625a98fb9310d012ed5fed8fa6f70b3bcfffb162b3ee59c021","body":{"detail":"Spec section 4.3 relies on no intercepted response carrying Access-Control-*; crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs:241 sends Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * on /_blob/, readable by any page's fetch if one slipped through. The plan has Task 15's lib/core/scheme.dart strip them; respond here and SchemeHost.kt's response() take any headers Dart gives. Dropping them natively, and refusing a 3xx there, makes the property hold whatever the Dart answerer does.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":181},"end":{"line":199},"content_hash":"100c2e2b9d17107b94f5fed76e777910d074f4daaddd9a85d319fe9474d7761b"},"summary":"Strip Access-Control-* in the native respond as well as in Dart: it is the one place every answer passes","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371197Z","id":"ae0319947ccb7115a3d4df20530035b3676c987e6b5a08d508641a78e396dabb","body":{"detail":"admits and allowed accept any path on clax://app in the main frame, and SchemeHost.kt numbers any main-frame request. A main-frame document at another shell path has the shell's origin, so it reaches ClaxHost natively (SchemeHost.swift:201-213 checks only main frame and origin) and only the nonce check stands. Today's other shell paths are /_blob/ (CSP sandbox), /_clax/ and /c/, so nothing a page controls runs there; restricting the policy keeps that true by construction.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"c4b651f67fe52a116f241926dc9505511c9ee1eac3bbee445adb3cd99ce0a957"},"suggested_fix":"Apple: cancel a main-frame shell-host navigation whose path does not start with /a/; Android: give no number to, and let Dart 403, a main-frame request outside /a/.","summary":"Allow main-frame navigations to the shell's host only for shell documents (/a/...), as spec section 4.2 says the app loads no other document there","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:26.140378Z","id":"4a7323ae497867cb10358f82f2f92c0cd11e1348ef7ad5e21bfd4d96c39784cd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:89bdc7263","summary":"Fixed in 89bdc7263: the permit no longer closes on the first matching request, so a frame's request for the shell's URL in the window takes the number beside the reload's own and costs it nothing. The race of 2a26c51f3, which lost the reload in 50 of 50 Mac runs with the one-shot permit, kept it in 50 of 50 with this fix (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_scheme_spike --runs_per_test=50 --nocache_test_results).","supersedes":"f3218c17f4d31eb4c02f8dc5d8452be9d79274b12171047123845a0453c581aa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:42.877395Z","id":"4647cbb933d76063ad7b4b250949f65558145083fbd87862ed4117853e632849","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9f3aa7559","summary":"Fixed in 9f3aa7559: SchemeHost.swift's respond (through SchemeHost.answer) and SchemeHost.kt's response() drop every Access-Control-* header. The spike's table now answers /api/artifacts with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *; before the fix the Mac spike read accessControlStripped false and apiUnreadable false (the content frame read 'read 200 {\"artifacts\":[\"secret\"]}'), after it both hold on the Mac (50 runs), the simulator and the Android emulator.","supersedes":"46cd022052a554625a98fb9310d012ed5fed8fa6f70b3bcfffb162b3ee59c021","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
